{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1210898-mistakes-from-the-past","id":1210898,"title":"Mistakes from the Past","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-24T04:47:26-07:00","id":1210898,"title":"Mistakes from the Past","content":"Anyone else find it odd, that you can turn lead into gold at arete 2, but you need arete 3 to engrave lead or gold?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23984-thkaal","name":"Thkaal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T05:23:56-07:00","id":1210908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thkaal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1210898-mistakes-from-the-past#post1210898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone else find it odd, that you can turn lead into gold at arete 2, but you need arete 3 to engrave lead or gold?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well you don't need Matter 3 to engrave a substance. You can just engrave it yourself.<br /> <br /> Matter places transmutations as being more simple than alterations in form. At Matter 2 you can turn solids into other solids, gases into other gases, liquids into other liquids, as long as you don't give it some special property which goes beyond simple transmutation.<br /> <br /> The reason transformations are rank 3 is that they have the capacity to be much more serious. You've given a rather mundane example; engraving. You don't need magick to do that. A chisel and Matter 1 for difficulty reductions will do. With Matter rank 3 you can turn a person's sword into smoke, cause the ceiling above someone's head to fall onto them by tearing it, fix a shattered circuit, turn a wall into thin air... it is much more powerful than any basic transmutation, such as turning wood to stone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T06:32:49-07:00","id":1210930,"title":"","content":"There has been a thread about this topic near the end of last year, which had an interesting discussion regading the Matter 2/3 order:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1170765-matter-question\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...atter-question</a><br /> <br /> Also, as Saikou hints at in the other thread, Matter 2 actually enables you to shape a hard substance easily, without resorting to Matter 3 or a chisel: in this case turn the gold into clay, reshape it and end the effect so it becomes gold again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 04-24-2018, 09:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T08:20:57-07:00","id":1211424,"title":"","content":"With Matter 2 I was under the impression something like engraving would be under that level. You wouldn't be able to change the total mass or anything, but I would say you could turn a long sword into a scimitar. At least that is the way I see it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19321-kewlimp","name":"kewlimp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T08:46:02-07:00","id":1211436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kewlimp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1210898-mistakes-from-the-past?p=1211424#post1211424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With Matter 2 I was under the impression something like engraving would be under that level. You wouldn't be able to change the total mass or anything, but I would say you could turn a long sword into a scimitar. At least that is the way I see it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You wouldn\u2019t be able to change the shape directly with Matter 2, but you can soften the blade, curve it and shape it yourself with a crafts roll, and then return it to steel.<br /> <br /> Matter 3 would allow the shape to change in an instance before your very eyes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}